"Summary (Verdict and Method Sketch) and Detailed Solution. The solution must be rigorous, with all steps justified, no gaps.\n\nWe need to determine all possible k for each n\u22653.\n\nWe have partially derived constraints: For even n, k \u2264 n-1 (cannot have all sunny lines). For odd n, maybe k can be n (all sunny) or maybe not. Let's explore further.\n\nWe need to find the exact set of possible k for each n.\n\nWe need to consider the covering problem more systematically.\n\nWe have N = n(n+1)/2 points. Each sunny line can contain at most M = floor((n+1)/2) points (proved earlier). Each unsunny line can contain at most n points (since the longest side length is n). Actually horizontal line y=b contains n+1-b points, which can be up to n (when b=1). Similarly vertical line x=a contains up to n points (when a=1). Slope -1 line x+y=s contains s-1 points, up to n (when s=n+1). So unsunny lines can cover at most n points.\n\nThus we have the inequality:\n\nu * n + k * M \u2265 N, where u = n - k.\n\nThus (n - k) * n + k * M \u2265 N.\n\nSimplify: n^2 - n k + k M \u2265 N => n^2 + k (M - n) \u2265 N.\n\nSince M \u2264 n (strictly less for n\u22653? Let's check: M = floor((n+1)/2). For n\u22653, M \u2264 n-1 (if n\u22653). Indeed, for n=3, M=2, n=3, M<n. For n=4, M=2, n=4, M<n. So M - n is negative. So the inequality gives an upper bound on k.\n\nRearrange: k (M - n) \u2265 N - n^2 => Since M - n < 0, dividing flips inequality:\n\nk \u2264 (n^2 - N) / (n - M).\n\nCompute n^2 - N = n^2 - n(n+1)/2 = n^2 - (n^2 + n)/2 = (2n^2 - n^2 - n)/2 = (n^2 - n)/2 = n(n-1)/2.\n\nThus k \u2264 [n(n-1)/2] / (n - M).\n\nNow compute denominator n - M.\n\nCase n even: n = 2t, M = t, n - M = t. So k \u2264 [2t(2t-1)/2] / t = [t(2t-1)] / t = 2t - 1 = n - 1. So k \u2264 n - 1. So for even n, k \u2264 n - 1.\n\nCase n odd: n = 2t+1, M = t+1, n - M = (2t+1) - (t+1) = t. So k \u2264 [ (2t+1)(2t)/2 ] / t = [ (2t+1) t ] / t = 2t+1 = n. So k \u2264 n. So no restriction beyond k \u2264 n (obvious